
--- testing ordinal of simple choice type: ---

0
1
2
3
ordinal is 0 for true
ordinal is 1 for 42
ordinal is 2 for 98
ordinal is 3 for hi

--- testing ordinals of some common choice types: ---

true .ordinal: 1 true expecting 1
false.ordinal: 0 false expecting 0
option String 'bla' .ordinal: 0 bla expecting 0
option String nil   .ordinal: 1 --nil-- expecting 1
option i64 42  .ordinal: 0 42 expecting 0
option i64 nil .ordinal: 1 --nil-- expecting 1

--- testing ordinals choice with several `void` entries: ---

id (choice unit void void) unit .ordinal 0 expecting 0
id (choice void unit void) unit .ordinal 1 expecting 1
id (choice void void unit) unit .ordinal 2 expecting 2
id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) 42   .ordinal: 3 42 expecting 3
id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) unit .ordinal: 6 unit expecting 6
id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) nil  .ordinal: 7 --nil-- expecting 7

--- testing `option nil`, which is effectively `choice nil nil`, but it can have ordinals 0 and 1: ---

id (Sequence nil) [nil] .first.ordinal: 0 expecting 0
id (Sequence nil) []    .first.ordinal: 1 expecting 1

--- choice of unit types and ref types only are encoded using not ordinal field but special ref values by the C backend: ---

id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) unit    .ordinal 0 expecting 0
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) 'str'   .ordinal 1 expecting 1
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) nil     .ordinal 2 expecting 2
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) [1,2,4] .ordinal 3 expecting 3
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) concur  .ordinal 4 expecting 4

--- choice of only unit types are treated like an int type by the JVM backend: ---

id (choice unit nil concur) unit   .ordinal 0 expecting 0
id (choice unit nil concur) nil    .ordinal 1 expecting 1
id (choice unit nil concur) concur .ordinal 2 expecting 2

--- testing with void alternatives ---

nil: 1 expecting 1

--- mix of void, several ref and several unit types ---

----blub----
1: StringYeahYeah!
2: nil
3: Sequence [1, 2, 3, 4]
4: unit

--- mix of void, one ref type, choice type and several unit types ---

----blob----
1: StringYeahYeah!
2: nil
3: option Sequence [1, 2, 3, 4]
4: unit
